  "body": "Follow-up from #42. In `Mode::Area`, law (b) (crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs) now measures every chord along its whole length. `Mode::Boundary` (Face, Contour, Thread, Drill, Bore) still reads a straight move only at its `to` (`laws::law_points`). So a Contour G1 cut across a convex corner of its own wall, with both ends R off it, is not convicted. The whole-chord reading cannot simply be switched on there: Face rows cross the face's open edge by design, and that convicted area_controls `face_extended_past_the_part_edge...` and `include_and_exclude_boundaries...`. Needs open-edge awareness: which region edges are walls and which are open.",
